#N canvas 20 20 4900 3820 12;
#X text 20 20 phase5-bench -- the Phase 5 acceptance run: clock \, transport \, the map and the LED. Ten seconds a step \, so you can watch the OLED and the aux button and mark each one off. Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch: it only pushes onto tempo \, param \, start \, stop and panic \, exactly as a controller would., f 110;
#X text 20 110 RUN IN THE FOREGROUND. Every step prints what it is sending and a PASS IF line -- including the steps whose correct result is that NOTHING happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark. Steps 1 to 11 drive themselves and 12 to 13 need your hands on the Organelle itself., f 110;
#X text 20 200 IT NEEDS -path POINTING AT THE PATCH FOLDER \, because it instantiates two c_clock objects and the deployed patch instantiates none. The by-hand console line in ref-conventions.md already carries -path for the patch folder -- on the Mac add -path "Cut It"., f 110;
#X text 20 290 NO COMMAS OR SEMICOLONS IN A PASS IF LINE. Both are message separators \, so one comma splits the string and the remainder lands somewhere unhelpful. phase3-bench and phase4-bench were both caught by this., f 110;
#X obj 4200 260 r \$0-say;
#X obj 4200 300 print;
#X obj 700 420 r clock;
#X obj 700 460 t b;
#X obj 700 500 f;
#X obj 700 540 + 1;
#X obj 840 580 t f f;
#X obj 840 650 f;
#X obj 1040 460 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 1040 500 0;
#X obj 1040 560 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 1040 600 0;
#X obj 700 650 r \$0-read;
#X obj 840 710 print M-BEATS;
#X obj 1700 340 c_clock 1 4;
#X obj 1700 460 t b;
#X obj 1700 500 f;
#X obj 1700 540 + 1;
#X obj 1840 580 t f f;
#X obj 1840 650 f;
#X obj 2040 460 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 2040 500 0;
#X obj 2040 560 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 2040 600 0;
#X obj 1700 650 r \$0-read;
#X obj 1840 710 print C1-BEATS-ratio-1;
#X obj 2700 340 c_clock 1.5 4;
#X obj 2700 460 t b;
#X obj 2700 500 f;
#X obj 2700 540 + 1;
#X obj 2840 580 t f f;
#X obj 2840 650 f;
#X obj 3040 460 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 3040 500 0;
#X obj 3040 560 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 3040 600 0;
#X obj 2700 650 r \$0-read;
#X obj 2840 710 print C2-BEATS-ratio-1.5;
#X text 700 800 THE TWO c_clock INSTANCES ARE WHAT STEPS 2 AND 3 EXIST FOR. Ratio 1 must land on exactly the same beats as the master reference and ratio 1.5 must produce half again as many -- under real DSP on the real device \, which is the one thing the Mac cannot prove. The deployed patch instantiates neither \, because nothing consumes a beat yet., f 100;
#X obj 140 1500 del 6000;
#X obj 240 1528 t b b;
#X msg 320 1566 === STEP-01-of-14 === baseline -- sending nothing;
#X obj 320 1596 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1566 PASS IF: two bars with a small gate mark under each and 120-bpm in the footer -- and the aux button lit DARK BLUE;
#X obj 1100 1596 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 1400 loadbang;
#X obj 140 1650 del 10000;
#X obj 240 1678 t b b b;
#X msg 320 1716 === STEP-02-of-14 === COUNTING -- zeroing the beat counters for 10 s at 120 BPM;
#X obj 320 1746 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1716 PASS IF: NOTHING VISIBLE CHANGES. The transport is still stopped and the clock is running anyway -- which is exactly what is being counted;
#X obj 1100 1746 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 1716 bang;
#X obj 2700 1746 s \$0-zero;
#X obj 140 1800 del 10000;
#X obj 240 1828 t b b b;
#X msg 320 1866 === STEP-03-of-14 === READ THE COUNTS -- the clock ran for 10 s while STOPPED;
#X obj 320 1896 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1866 PASS IF: M-BEATS 20 or 21 -- C1-BEATS the same number -- C2-BEATS 30 or 31. A zero anywhere means the clock does not run until the transport does -- or on the Mac it means DSP is off which looks exactly the same;
#X obj 1100 1896 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 1866 bang;
#X obj 2700 1896 s \$0-read;
#X obj 140 1950 del 10000;
#X obj 240 1978 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2016 === STEP-04-of-14 === START THE TRANSPORT;
#X obj 320 2046 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2016 PASS IF: the aux button turns GREEN and the 404 starts running -- and its tempo display still reads 120;
#X obj 1100 2046 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2016 bang;
#X obj 2700 2046 s start;
#X obj 140 2100 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2128 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2166 === STEP-05-of-14 === TEMPO THROUGH THE MAP -- og-knob-1 at 0;
#X obj 320 2196 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2166 PASS IF: the footer reads 60-bpm and the 404's own tempo follows within a second or two. THIS IS THE REAL done-when;
#X obj 1100 2196 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2166 og-knob-1 0;
#X obj 2700 2196 s param;
#X obj 140 2250 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2278 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2316 === STEP-06-of-14 === TEMPO THROUGH THE MAP -- og-knob-1 at 1;
#X obj 320 2346 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2316 PASS IF: the footer reads 180-bpm and the 404 follows again. It may stutter on the way -- a big jump is inferred over several pulses and that is documented rather than broken;
#X obj 1100 2346 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2316 og-knob-1 1;
#X obj 2700 2346 s param;
#X obj 140 2400 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2428 t b b b b;
#X msg 320 2466 === STEP-07-of-14 === OUT OF RANGE -- 500 sent TWICE;
#X obj 320 2496 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2466 PASS IF: the footer reads 300-bpm and EXACTLY ONE alert appears. The second 500 must be silent -- a warning per message is a flood rather than a report;
#X obj 1100 2496 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2466 500;
#X obj 2700 2496 s tempo;
#X msg 3200 2466 500;
#X obj 3200 2496 s tempo;
#X obj 140 2550 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2578 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2616 === STEP-08-of-14 === BACK TO 120;
#X obj 320 2646 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2616 PASS IF: the footer reads 120-bpm and NO alert appears at all;
#X obj 1100 2646 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2616 120;
#X obj 2700 2646 s tempo;
#X obj 140 2700 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2728 t b b b b;
#X msg 320 2766 === STEP-09-of-14 === STOP -- and the clock must NOT stop with it;
#X obj 320 2796 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2766 PASS IF: the aux button goes DARK BLUE and the 404 stops -- the counters are zeroed here and the next step must still show about 20;
#X obj 1100 2796 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2766 bang;
#X obj 2700 2796 s \$0-zero;
#X msg 3200 2766 bang;
#X obj 3200 2796 s stop;
#X obj 140 2850 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2878 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2916 === STEP-10-of-14 === READ THE COUNTS WHILE STOPPED;
#X obj 320 2946 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2916 PASS IF: M-BEATS 20 or 21 again. Stop the pulse stream and the 404 stretches every sample to a stale tempo -- so this is the least obvious requirement in the phase;
#X obj 1100 2946 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2916 bang;
#X obj 2700 2946 s \$0-read;
#X obj 140 3000 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3028 t b b b;
#X msg 320 3066 === STEP-11-of-14 === PANIC;
#X obj 320 3096 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3066 PASS IF: the aux button turns RED and the footer says panic -- and the clock is STILL running underneath;
#X obj 1100 3096 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 3066 bang;
#X obj 2700 3096 s panic;
#X obj 140 3150 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3178 t b b;
#X msg 320 3216 === STEP-12-of-14 === BY HAND -- press the aux button twice;
#X obj 320 3246 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3216 PASS IF: the first press turns it GREEN and starts the 404 and the second turns it DARK BLUE and stops it. If nothing happens at all then mother is eating the press -- check that before suspecting u_map;
#X obj 1100 3246 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 3300 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3328 t b b;
#X msg 320 3366 === STEP-13-of-14 === BY HAND -- sweep KNOB 1 all the way and back;
#X obj 320 3396 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3366 PASS IF: og-knob-1 appears as a parameter row on the OLED and the footer tracks between 60-bpm and 180-bpm. The 404 follows the sweep;
#X obj 1100 3396 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 3450 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3478 t b b;
#X msg 320 3516 === STEP-14-of-14 === done -- press Ctrl-C;
#X obj 320 3546 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3516 PASS IF: every step above was marked off. If 2 3 9 or 10 failed the clock is wrong -- if 5 6 or 13 failed the map is -- if 4 11 or 12 failed the transport or the LED is;
#X obj 1100 3546 s \$0-say;
